  "date_basis": "chunk_manifest",
  "concise_summary": "PKD constructs a Neoplatonic and Dantean hierarchical cosmology of three ontological realms (hell, purgatorio, paradiso) structured on a vertical axis to reinterpret his 2-3-74 visionary experience. Drawing on Malebranche's occasionalism and divine illumination, he argues that the ordinary world is self-generated illusion from which we must cease fleeing temporally and instead confront annihilation to access the truly-other (God/Valis/Logos). Christ's invasion from outside shatters the private maze-world and restores consciousness of the eternal interconnected structure of divine ideas.",
  "key_claims": [
    "The perceived world is self-generated and irreal because we generate it through our own minds; we experience our own thought-formations coming back to us as world",
    "All existential realms exist simultaneously in a Dantean vertical hierarchy (hell, purgatorio, paradiso), not in temporal sequence; we occupy the middle realm in relation to proximity to or distance from God",
    "Ceasing to flee through time and confronting Heidegger's annihilating Fate directly causes the irreal world to freeze and give way to the wholly-other (God), a transformation from knowing the false other to knowing the true other",
    "Christ's appearance from outside the maze-world (e.g., the Golden Fish sign) proves the existence of a real world not autogenerated by the perceiver; it breaks the enclosure of the private mind",
    "In Malebranche's system, God compels our assent to representations through direct illumination; we and world are both in God, making any experience of the cosmos as sacred body a vision of literal reality, not metaphor",
    "A vast teleological causation operates beneath apparent causation, where ostensibly trivial causes are pre-wound masks concealing divine purposes determined by an omniscient artisan-God with perfect foresight"
  ],
