  "literary_self_ref": [
    "VALIS is basically correct in its depiction of the maze, Grail, plasmate, and living information",
    "The character King Felix embodies the principle of how living information (the blood) aids us",
    "The novel's structure maps the theological reality: Christ as map, template as map of the maze",
    "The Acts lens/grid functions as a hermeneutical map of reality itself",
    "PKD's binary switching system with perpetual disjunctions is superior to the corpus Christi mysticism as a theological discovery"
  ],
  "symbols_images": [
    "The Maze - the self-generated irreal world of perception from which we flee",
    "The Grail - the source of living information and clues to navigate the maze",
    "The Golden Christian Fish - sign invading from outside, shattering the private world",
    "Blood/Plasmate - living information that speaks to us and provides guidance",
    "The Black Iron Prison (BIP) - the lowest realm, total encapsulation",
    "Heaven/Upper realm - world gives way to God, paradiso",
    "Hell - total encapsulation with no world and no other",
    "The Rose/Roses - Dantean symbol of divine beauty and order (Heaven as rose, Earth as rose particulars)",
    "Medieval Gothic vertical spatial axis - the hierarchy of being connecting upper and lower realms",
    "Horizontal flight in time - ineffectual running away from Fate down the time-corridor"
  ],
  "tensions": [
    "The paradox that the irreal world is better than none at all, yet worse than heaven and cut off from God",
    "God compels assent to representations while claiming we are free; how can representation be both absolutely compelled and constitute genuine experience?",
    "If world is generated by our minds, how can Christ's invasion from outside break this enclosure?",
    "The self-refutation problem: to comprehend the world as irreal is simultaneously to escape it, yet we cannot escape while trapped in it",
    "Malebranche's occasionalism denies causation in creatures but then what is the ontological status of the creature's will?",
    "Claiming superiority of binary switching/causation-as-selection over corpus Christi mysticism undermines the preceding Malebranchian framework",
    "The teleological causal system assumes perfect foresight, but then what is the nature of the creature's free choice in triggering consequences?"
  ],
  "evidence_quotes": [
    "Our world is irreal + we generate it ourselves (+ for precisely this reason it can properly be called irreal;) thus in contact with it we experience not the true other but in fact our own thought-formations spun out of our own minds, coming back at us as world.",
    "The best term for Valis is Rudolf Otto's: 'the wholly other.' This could also be described as an ascent from ignorance + slavery to knowledge + freedom.",
    "Once thus confronted, world freezes + then becomes -is revealed as or gives way to- the wholly other, the true (authentic) other. (This is Buber's conversion from it to thou.)",
    "We are really still there, but are perceptually + cognitively blind. Under these blinded circumstances God supplies us a world derived chiefly from our own minds; it is both a blessing (in that it is a world we do take to be real); + a punishment (in that we are cut off from God + in a private world, so-to-speak alone - without him).",
    "Christ intervening from outside our private world; he must literally invade it + help us; on our own we cannot extricate ourselves."
  ],
  "uncertainty_flags": [
    "The illustration referenced (maze diagram, heaven/rose/eidos diagram) is not preserved in text; exact symbolic meaning unclear",
    "Reference to 'folder 90-159' and folder references throughout suggest PKD is citing his own archival manuscripts; sources not independently verified",
    "The 'legend of the Pearl' mentioned in context of anamnesis - unclear if PKD means Thomas's Hymn of the Pearl, Gnostic texts, or his own coinage",
    "The nature of PKD's 'narrowly-defined highly specific act' causing restoration from exile remains unexplained",
    "The claim that transubstantiation was 'literally real' in medieval thinking conflates theological metaphor with phenomenological claim",
    "Jane Burton's identity and relationship to PKD unclear; the diagram drawing is mentioned but not described",
    "Whether the Malebranchian framework or the binary switching/causation-as-selection framework represents PKD's actual theology is unresolved"
  ],
